From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: add the CPU power-down idle state

TF-A (nuubOS patches 0001/0002) implements the H616 native PSCI
CPU_SUSPEND power-down state 0x00010000 (cluster and system stay on),
but no idle state was described, so idle cores only ran WFI. With it the
cores of an idle H700 (RG CubeXX, Home, screen on) are powered down 78 %
of the time (92 % with the screen off). Qualified on the CubeXX: deep
sleep/resume, heavy emulation (God of War PSP, same fps), no kernel errors.
local-timer-stop: the per-CPU timer is lost while powered down (the
sun8i-a23 timer is the broadcast device).

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -23,6 +23,22 @@
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
 
+		idle-states {
+			entry-method = "psci";
+
+			/* CPU power down (TF-A native PSCI CPU_SUSPEND, state
+			 * 0x00010000 as the vendor firmware): cluster and
+			 * system stay on. */
+			cpu_sleep: cpu-sleep-0 {
+				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00010000>;
+				local-timer-stop;
+				entry-latency-us = <100>;
+				exit-latency-us = <500>;
+				min-residency-us = <5000>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		cpu0: cpu@0 {
 			compatible = "arm,cortex-a53";
 			device_type = "cpu";
@@ -37,6 +53,7 @@
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>;
 		};
 
 		cpu1: cpu@1 {
@@ -53,6 +70,7 @@
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>;
 		};
 
 		cpu2: cpu@2 {
@@ -69,6 +87,7 @@
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>;
 		};
 
 		cpu3: cpu@3 {
@@ -85,6 +104,7 @@
 			d-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			d-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&l2_cache>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep>;
 		};
 
 		l2_cache: l2-cache {
